#N canvas 40 60 1280 1010 12;
#X declare -path ..;
#X obj 0 0 cnv 1 1280 46 empty empty 11\ \ \ Autoencoders\ and\ VAEs\ \ -\ \ a\ latent\ space\ of\ timbres\ (2006\ /\ 2013) 14 23 0 20 #1d3557 #ffffff 0;
#X obj 1110 980 declare -path ..;
#X text 800 980 finds the nn.* objects one folder up ->, f 42;
#X text 20 980 neuralplay - Moisés Horta Valenzuela / SEMILLA.AI Studio, f 70;
#X text 20 56 An AUTOENCODER squeezes data through a bottleneck and learns to rebuild it. The bottleneck - here just 2 numbers - becomes a MAP of the data: the LATENT SPACE. This one was trained on 8 timbres. Move through the map and listen to the network invent the sounds in between., f 175;
#X obj 10 96 cnv 1 390 890 empty empty THE\ IDEA 8 12 0 13 #eef1f5 #1d3557 0;
#X text 20 122 ENCODER: input -> fewer and fewer neurons -> a tiny code. DECODER: code -> more neurons -> the input again. Trained to make output = input \, the network must find the essence of the data to squeeze it through (Hinton and Salakhutdinov \, 2006)., f 52;
#X text 20 218 Here a timbre is 8 numbers (the loudness of 8 harmonics). The code is 2 numbers = a point on a map. Similar timbres end up close together., f 52;
#X text 20 269 VARIATIONAL autoencoder (Kingma and Welling \, 2013): the encoder gives a REGION \, not a point - a mean mu and a spread sigma. Training samples z = mu + sigma * noise (the "reparameterisation trick") and adds a penalty (KL divergence) that keeps all regions near the centre. Result: a smooth map without holes - every point decodes into something sensible., f 52;
#X text 20 395 This is the idea behind RAVE (Caillon and Esling \, 2021) \, the realtime audio VAE you can run in Pd with [nn~]: a learned latent space of raw sound you can play like an instrument., f 52;
#X text 20 461 TRAINING happens in Python (python/train_vae.py \, 8 timbres \, 6000 steps of gradient descent with backpropagation \, about 2 seconds). Pd only RUNS the trained network - the same split as RAVE and [nn~]. Change the timbres in the script \, retrain \, reopen this lesson., f 52;
#X text 20 557 NOTE: the original NeuralNetwork-VAE patch had the shape of an autoencoder with random weights. A real VAE is trained \, and that is what makes its latent space meaningful., f 52;
#X obj 410 96 cnv 1 430 520 empty empty THE\ LATENT\ MAP\ \ (z1\ left-right\,\ z2\ down-up) 8 12 0 13 #e3f0fb #1d3557 0;
#X obj 470 150 cnv 1 240 240 empty empty empty 4 10 0 12 #ffffff #000000 0;
#X obj 590 150 cnv 1 1 240 empty empty empty 4 10 0 12 #d0d0d0 #000000 0;
#X obj 470 270 cnv 1 240 1 empty empty empty 4 10 0 12 #d0d0d0 #000000 0;
#X obj 586 266 cnv 1 8 8 empty \$0-pm0 sine 10 4 0 10 #1d3557 #1d3557 0;
#X obj 586 266 cnv 1 8 8 empty \$0-pm1 saw 10 4 0 10 #1d3557 #1d3557 0;
#X obj 586 266 cnv 1 8 8 empty \$0-pm2 square 10 4 0 10 #1d3557 #1d3557 0;
#X obj 586 266 cnv 1 8 8 empty \$0-pm3 triangle 10 4 0 10 #1d3557 #1d3557 0;
#X obj 586 266 cnv 1 8 8 empty \$0-pm4 organ 10 4 0 10 #1d3557 #1d3557 0;
#X obj 586 266 cnv 1 8 8 empty \$0-pm5 hollow 10 4 0 10 #1d3557 #1d3557 0;
#X obj 586 266 cnv 1 8 8 empty \$0-pm6 bright 10 4 0 10 #1d3557 #1d3557 0;
#X obj 586 266 cnv 1 8 8 empty \$0-pm7 odd 10 4 0 10 #1d3557 #1d3557 0;
