#N canvas 40 60 1200 700 the-vae 0;
#X text 20 10 THE NETWORK \, made of [nn.dense] layers. All numbers live in arrays named v<\$0>_... (the \$0 keeps them private to this patch). The weights are text files in lessons/data/vae/ \, written by python/train_vae.py and read into the arrays at load., f 150;
#X obj 20 80 array define v\$0_x 8;
#X obj 250 80 array define v\$0_eh 16;
#X obj 480 80 array define v\$0_eh_w 128;
#X obj 710 80 array define v\$0_eh_b 16;
#X obj 940 80 array define v\$0_mu 2;
#X obj 20 106 array define v\$0_mu_w 32;
#X obj 250 106 array define v\$0_mu_b 2;
#X obj 480 106 array define v\$0_lv 2;
#X obj 710 106 array define v\$0_lv_w 32;
#X obj 940 106 array define v\$0_lv_b 2;
#X obj 20 132 array define v\$0_z 2;
#X obj 250 132 array define v\$0_dh 16;
#X obj 480 132 array define v\$0_dh_w 32;
#X obj 710 132 array define v\$0_dh_b 16;
#X obj 940 132 array define v\$0_y_w 128;
#X obj 20 158 array define v\$0_y_b 8;
#X text 20 200 ENCODER: spectrum x (8) -> 16 tanh neurons -> mean mu (2) and log-variance lv (2) of the latent point, f 120;
#X obj 20 230 r \$0-encode;
#X obj 20 260 nn.dense v\$0_x v\$0_eh tanh;
#X obj 20 290 t b b;
#X obj 260 320 nn.dense v\$0_eh v\$0_lv linear;
#X obj 20 320 nn.dense v\$0_eh v\$0_mu linear;
#X obj 20 350 s \$0-encoded;
#X text 20 400 DECODER: latent point z (2) -> 16 tanh neurons -> spectrum y (8) \, sigmoid so every partial is 0..1, f 120;
#X obj 20 430 r \$0-decode;
#X obj 20 460 nn.dense v\$0_z v\$0_dh tanh;
#X obj 20 490 nn.dense v\$0_dh v\$0_y sigmoid;
#X obj 20 520 s \$0-decoded;
#X text 300 460 2 x 16 + 16 x 8 = 160 multiply-adds: cheap enough to run every time you move the map, f 40;
#X obj 700 200 r \$0-loadweights;
#X obj 700 226 t b b b b b b b b b b;
